1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,360
Hi, I'm Zeke.

2
00:00:01,360 --> 00:00:05,590
About 70,000 people in the U.S. died of an overdose last year.

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,450
Three in four of them were alone.

4
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:10,160
An overdose slows your breathing,

5
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:11,100
then it stops.

6
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:12,280
And if nobody's there,

7
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,220
no one knows.

8
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:16,100
I built BreathBuddy so somebody does and

9
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:17,650
can come to help.

10
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:19,640
A friend sets it up in just

11
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:21,680
a minute and texts you a link.

12
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:22,980
There's nothing to install,

13
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:24,550
it's just a web app.

14
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:25,900
You open it,

15
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,850
press start, and breathe with the cloud.

16
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:30,500
The speaker plays a sound too high

17
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:31,360
for you to hear,

18
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:33,500
and the microphone listens for the echo

19
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:34,460
off your chest.

20
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:36,720
Those slow breaths show it where you

21
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:37,560
are.

22
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:40,060
Now it's locked onto my chest.

23
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:41,740
It knows where my chest is and

24
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:42,840
how much it moves when I breathe

25
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:43,890
normally.

26
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:46,330
Now I hold my breath.

27
00:00:49,020 --> 00:00:50,990
And after a few seconds,

28
00:00:51,020 --> 00:00:53,070
it asks out loud.

29
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:56,600
And after six seconds,

30
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:59,220
it calls my emergency contact through Twilio.

31
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:01,440
And an ElevenLabs voice agent explains what

32
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:02,920
happened and tells them exactly where I

33
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:03,970
am.

34
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:13,370
When they pick up,

35
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:15,370
they hear my location.

36
00:01:15,380 --> 00:01:16,260
If they miss it,

37
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:17,460
they can ask and the agent tells

38
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:18,510
them again.

39
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:20,420
It asks them to call 911 or

40
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:21,540
get to me as fast as they

41
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:22,590
can.

42
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:25,460
Here's what it actually sees.

43
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:28,580
This is my chest moving as I

44
00:01:28,580 --> 00:01:29,520
breathe.

45
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:31,640
This morning, it caught 11 out of

46
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:33,690
11 breath holds live.

47
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:35,600
On some hard recordings from yesterday when

48
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:36,670
I was moving around,

49
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:38,260
it caught 23 out of 29.

50
00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:41,160
But that was before fully tuning the

51
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:43,270
slow breathing lock-in.

52
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:45,960
That's only results with me with my

53
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:46,740
laptop.

54
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:48,080
So to expand this,

55
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:50,020
I would need to collect much more

56
00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:52,560
data from other people breathing and other

57
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:54,540
devices from iPhone,

58
00:01:54,540 --> 00:01:56,160
Android, and other things.

59
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:57,920
Next, I want to be able to

60
00:01:57,920 --> 00:02:01,380
reliably catch breathing that's slowing down on

61
00:02:01,380 --> 00:02:03,780
any device and be able to accurately

62
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:05,080
report the exact rate.

63
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:07,220
And this is an experimental prototype.

64
00:02:07,220 --> 00:02:09,020
It's only been tested on me so

65
00:02:09,020 --> 00:02:12,500
far with my laptop and my phone.

66
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:13,840
But it runs on the browser,

67
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:16,740
so it takes no setup to install

68
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:22,160
and can instantly call someone to give

69
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:24,210
someone who overdoses another chance.

